Z||000004||AusFiero||07-29-2001||07:53 PM||||Oh I will be definately telling them about here. Plus they don't have a web site. They will now. I am about to ring them and join now.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||07-29-2001||08:11 PM||||Oh bummer,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> club got disolved about 3 years ago I just found out when I rang the contact number. <P>But it has given me some incentive to start one. So I spoke to Dave at Ponti-World Australia and he has put me onto 12 Fiero owners within an hours drive of my place.<P>Including a Fiero mad husband and wife team that both drive Fieros. I think they alone will be a good starting point to start a club. <P>Hey guess what else I found. A guy here has an 88 GT with every factory option including t-tops and only 16000 miles on the clock. Surely he will join the club.<P>Ok I have never started a Car Club before. Any hints and tips from people running ones now would really help me out? I want this to be a good social friendly club. Not a political, power junkie filled club like our Pontiac Car Club of Australia is now.<P>Any tips from people running Fieo Clubs now would be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||07-29-2001||08:27 PM||||One thing I am learning, Jim... I started our club and made it free for all. I was eating all of the costs and only wanted people to participate, but we slowly lose contact with more and more people and only have our few loyals...<P>I have heard all of my life that people are more willing to participate if they have a stake in something... therefore, we are going to have dues like most other clubs just to get people that we know are interested. Of course, I have to make sure they get at least $10 worth of value.. but that won't be a problem.<P>Another thing that I am learning... don't try to do everything yourself. Let the other people get involved. It makes things easier and also more fun.<P>Good luck with your club...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||6
Z||000007||Fierochic88||07-30-2001||11:07 AM||||Hey Aus -<BR> Keep us posted on your progress!<P>Jennifer<P><P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||07-30-2001||11:54 AM||||You know from reading the replies to this topic you lot have given me a great idea for a name for the club.<P>Fieros Down Under ...sounds pretty cool to me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Plus I can get some great domain names out of it too. You have to be a club or businss to register domain names in Australia and they must be relevant to the club or business. So watch out for <A HREF="http://www.fiero.com.au" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.com.au</A>  and <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org.au" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.org.au</A>  Well as long as I can convince at least some of the Fiero owners to join and help me run it.||||reg||1
